---
description: Playwright E2E patterns for the salary-run app
globs: tests/**/*.spec.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

Auto-attached whenever a spec file is in context.

## Required scaffolding

```typescript
test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/');
  await page.evaluate(() => localStorage.clear());
  await page.reload();
});
```

## Canonical interactions

```typescript
// Add an employee
await page.getByTestId('name-input').fill('Anna Karlsson');
await page.getByTestId('kennitala-input').fill('120375-2029');
await page.getByTestId('salary-input').fill('750000');
await page.getByTestId('add-employee').click();

// Rows
await expect(page.locator('.employee-row')).toHaveCount(1);
await expect(page.locator('.name-cell')).toHaveText('Anna Karlsson');

// Mark as paid (include in the run)
await page.locator('.employee-row', { hasText: 'Anna' }).getByRole('checkbox').check();

// Run totals — compare the formatted string, not a parsed number
await expect(page.getByTestId('total-net')).toHaveText('720.500 kr.');

// Seed state directly — faster than the UI for preconditions
await page.evaluate(() => {
  localStorage.setItem('payday-employees', JSON.stringify([
    { id: '1', name: 'Erik Lindberg', kennitala: '0101902079', salary: 600000, paid: false },
  ]));
});
await page.reload();
```

## Stable test ids in this app

`name-input`, `kennitala-input`, `salary-input`, `add-employee`, `form-error`,
`empty-state`, `period-input`, `period-label`, `run-count`, `total-gross`, `total-net`,
`clear-paid`.

Rows expose classes, not ids: `.employee-row`, `.name-cell`, `.kennitala-cell`,
`.net-cell`, `.remove-btn`, `td.num`. If a test needs a new hook, add a `data-testid`
to `main.js` rather than reaching for a CSS chain.

## Assertion habits that catch real payroll defects

- Assert the **row total and the run total together**. A rounding defect only shows when
  you compare the sum of rows against the displayed total.
- Assert **both sides of a threshold** when a calculation has bands, one krona apart.
- Assert **the formatted string** so locale and rounding defects cannot hide.
- For accessibility, prefer `await expect(page.locator('main')).toMatchAriaSnapshot(...)`
  over hand-written structural assertions.
